Graph 1: Scatter Plot (Daily Exercise vs Stress)

Even with binary exercise, this works.

import pandas as pd
import seaborn as sns
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

df = pd.read_csv("daily_exercise_stress.csv")

plt.figure(figsize=(7,5))
sns.scatterplot(
    data=df,
    x="Exercise",
    y="Stress",
    jitter=0.1
)

plt.xticks([0,1], ["No Exercise", "Exercise"])
plt.title("Daily Exercise vs Stress Level")
plt.ylabel("Stress Level (1–5)")
plt.show()

Graph 2: Line Plot (Stress Over Time)

This becomes very powerful visually.

plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))
plt.plot(df["Day"], df["Stress"], marker='o')

plt.title("Daily Stress Levels Over Time")
plt.xlabel("Day")
plt.ylabel("Stress Level (1–5)")
plt.show()

Extra (Highly Recommended): Mean Stress Comparison

This is simple and looks great.

mean_stress = df.groupby("Exercise")["Stress"].mean()

mean_stress.plot(kind="bar", color=["tomato", "seagreen"])
plt.xticks([0,1], ["No Exercise", "Exercise"], rotation=0)
plt.title("Average Stress on Exercise vs Non-Exercise Days")
plt.ylabel("Average Stress Level")
plt.show()

